    <h3>How long does a sweepstakes casino redemption take?</h3>
    <p>By published terms, roughly 2 days to 7 business days depending on operator and method. Chumba Casino processes within 2 days of approval, Pulsz quotes 3-7 business days for a first redemption, and McLuck quotes 2-5 days by bank transfer after up to 72 hours of processing. First redemptions are slower because verification runs first.</p>
    <h3>Why is my first redemption slower?</h3>
    <p>It triggers identity verification. The operator checks your ID against your registered details and payment method before releasing funds; verified accounts skip most of this on later redemptions.</p>
    <h3>What is the minimum redemption at each operator?</h3>
    <p>Stake.us requires a minimum of 40 SC. McLuck requires 75 SC for bank transfer or 10 SC for a gift card. Minimums for other operators are listed in their terms of service.</p>
    <h3>What delays a sweepstakes casino redemption?</h3>
    <p>The common causes are incomplete identity verification, a name or address mismatch between your ID and your account, an incomplete wagering requirement on Sweeps Coins, and requests made over weekends or holidays when payment rails do not settle.</p>
